# NJ Coast — Project Rules for Cursor

## What this project is
A scenic locations finder for **Cape May County, New Jersey**, deployed as a static site on GitHub Pages at **njcoast.me**. Users explore beaches, wildlife refuges, lighthouses, parks, and marshes on an interactive map powered by Google Maps, with an AI guide powered by Gemini 2.0 Flash.

## Stack
- **Vite 8 + React 19** — static site, no SSR
- **React Router v7** — client-side routing (`/` → MapPage, `/about` → AboutPage)
- **PostHog** — product analytics via `posthog-js/react` `PostHogProvider`
- **Google Maps** — `@vis.gl/react-google-maps` with `AdvancedMarker` + `InfoWindow`
- **Gemini AI** — `@google/generative-ai`, model `gemini-2.0-flash`, streaming chat
- **Vertex AI Search** — Discovery Engine REST API (covered by GenAI App Builder credit)
- **Doppler** — secrets management (`doppler run -- npm run dev` locally; `DOPPLER_TOKEN` in CI)

## File layout
```
src/
  services/
    gemini.js          # Gemini 2.0 Flash wrapper (streamSceneryChat, generateLocationSpotlight)
    vertexSearch.js    # Vertex AI Search REST wrapper (searchLocations, rankLocations)
  data/
    scenicLocations.js # 12 curated Cape May County locations + CATEGORIES constant
    mapStyle.js        # COASTAL_MAP_STYLE — inline JSON fallback when no Map ID is set
  components/
    NavBar.jsx / .css
    AiAssistant.jsx / .css  # Floating chat panel, Gemini-powered
  pages/
    MapPage.jsx / .css      # Main map view with sidebar + AI assistant
    AboutPage.jsx / .css
  App.jsx / .css            # Router, PostHog pageview tracking
  main.jsx                  # PostHogProvider init, BrowserRouter
  index.css                 # Design tokens (--navy, --ocean, --gold, --sand, --marsh)
```

## Secrets & env vars
All secrets go through Doppler. The canonical reference is `.env.example`.
Never hardcode keys. Always use `import.meta.env.VITE_*`.

Key vars:
- `VITE_POSTHOG_KEY` / `VITE_POSTHOG_HOST`
- `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` — Maps JS API key, domain-restricted to njcoast.me
- `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID` — Cloud Map ID for custom Cape May styling + AdvancedMarker
- `VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY` — Gemini API key (Google AI Studio or Google Cloud)
- `VITE_VERTEX_SEARCH_PROJECT_ID` / `VITE_VERTEX_SEARCH_LOCATION` / `VITE_VERTEX_SEARCH_DATA_STORE` / `VITE_VERTEX_SEARCH_API_KEY`

## Design tokens (index.css)
```
--navy   #0b2e54   brand dark
--ocean  #1a6fa8   brand blue / primary interactive
--gold   #e8c87c   accent (navbar border, highlights)
--sand   #f4a261   beach / warm category color
--marsh  #52b788   wildlife / green category color
```
Dark mode is supported via `prefers-color-scheme: dark`.

## Coding conventions
- **Functional components only** — no class components
- **useCallback** for all event handlers passed to children or used in effects
- **PostHog capture** on every meaningful user interaction (category filter, location select, AI queries)
- CSS is **component-scoped** plain CSS files (no CSS modules, no Tailwind)
- No TypeScript — plain JSX/JS
- No `console.log` in committed code
- Graceful degradation: every service that needs an API key must render a helpful fallback UI when the key is missing

## Google Maps custom style
- `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID` → cloud-based styling (user creates in Cloud Console)
- When not set, `COASTAL_MAP_STYLE` from `src/data/mapStyle.js` is used as inline styles
- `mapTypeId` prop enables roadmap/satellite/hybrid/terrain switching
- Custom style only applies in `roadmap` mode; satellite/hybrid show aerial imagery

